1
00:00:18,133 --> 00:00:19,935
Florence is really a fool.

2
00:00:19,935 --> 00:00:22,404
Because of her, our Agora day is extended.

3
00:00:22,404 --> 00:00:25,840
You know, we should be supporting her.

4
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,812
I'm not saying we will not support her.

5
00:00:28,812 --> 00:00:32,614
But does she have a realistic chance
against Camille?

6
00:00:32,614 --> 00:00:36,685
With what we're about to do,
that girl will stand no chance.

7
00:00:36,685 --> 00:00:38,320
We will ruin her.

8
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,788
We will destroy her.

9
00:00:39,788 --> 00:00:43,558
I now present to you, Camille and Florence.

10
00:00:43,558 --> 00:00:48,763
Do you think she is worthy
to be your Com Arts representative?

11
00:00:48,763 --> 00:00:50,738
Bea?

12
00:00:52,870 --> 00:00:54,354
Ooh.

13
00:00:54,354 --> 00:00:56,805
Next.

14
00:00:56,805 --> 00:00:59,607
Camille, that's not true.

15
00:00:59,607 --> 00:01:02,944
I, for a fact, wanted to be her friend too.

16
00:01:02,944 --> 00:01:06,014
But yesterday, I saw her.

17
00:01:06,014 --> 00:01:08,589
I saw her making a fool of herself.

18
00:01:08,589 --> 00:01:12,291
Is that the representative that you want?

19
00:01:13,488 --> 00:01:15,824
Someone who is so messed up.

20
00:01:15,824 --> 00:01:21,496
Oh my, she might mess up something
in the student body.

21
00:01:21,496 --> 00:01:25,803
So, if you guys still don't believe
that I should be the Com Arts representative,

22
00:01:25,803 --> 00:01:27,638
don't let the face

23
00:01:27,638 --> 00:01:32,647
of one of the most dynamic departments
of this university

24
00:01:32,647 --> 00:01:36,444
be someone with questionable morals.

25
00:01:37,334 --> 00:01:41,106
She doesn't deserve
to be your representative.

26
00:01:41,106 --> 00:01:43,575
She doesn't even deserve
to be in this school.

27
00:01:43,575 --> 00:01:45,644
It's impossible that you saw her yesterday,

28
00:01:45,644 --> 00:01:48,947
because we were together yesterday.

29
00:01:48,947 --> 00:01:52,284
Why are you together? Do you even know her?

30
00:01:52,284 --> 00:01:53,545
She's my girlfriend.

31
00:01:53,545 --> 00:01:55,254
Oh my God...

32
00:01:55,254 --> 00:01:57,523
You're kidding, right?

33
00:01:57,523 --> 00:02:03,095
So, you're saying you know this woman,
and you're in a relationship?

34
00:02:03,095 --> 00:02:06,131
So, are you saying the Ferells are liars?

35
00:02:06,131 --> 00:02:07,833
Accusing us of lying is something our family

36
00:02:07,833 --> 00:02:10,502
won't let you get away with it.

37
00:02:10,502 --> 00:02:13,036
Because the Ferells are many things.

38
00:02:13,036 --> 00:02:17,220
But to lie, we can't do that.

39
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:20,846
You know, that's enough.

40
00:02:20,846 --> 00:02:23,008
Let's proceed to vote.

41
00:02:27,281 --> 00:02:29,088
Camille, stop!

42
00:02:29,088 --> 00:02:31,090
I hate her!

43
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:33,048
Why is she doing this to me?

44
00:02:33,048 --> 00:02:36,328
Why is this happening?

45
00:02:36,328 --> 00:02:38,492
What are you looking at?

46
00:02:44,002 --> 00:02:46,952
Ms. Villarico, can I talk to you?

47
00:02:49,441 --> 00:02:51,109
Dean?

48
00:03:48,834 --> 00:03:51,103
Girlfriend, cook.

49
00:03:51,103 --> 00:03:52,971
Tomatoes, tomatoes.

50
00:03:52,971 --> 00:03:54,640
Potatoes, potatoes.

51
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,632
It seems there's not much difference.

52
00:03:56,632 --> 00:03:58,710
What do you mean there's not much difference?

53
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:03,482
I mean, you cook for Nero,
you take care of him.

54
00:04:03,482 --> 00:04:07,252
You live in his house
and you even went on a date on the farm.

55
00:04:07,252 --> 00:04:12,324
Not to mention, if you get mad,
you burn down his bat cave.

56
00:04:12,324 --> 00:04:16,957
Technically, it falls under
the definition of a girlfriend,

57
00:04:16,957 --> 00:04:18,656
almost wife too.

58
00:04:18,656 --> 00:04:21,736
Exactly. And to be fair,
I want what Nero did,

59
00:04:21,736 --> 00:04:23,952
to call you his girlfriend instead of a cook.

60
00:04:23,952 --> 00:04:27,468
It gives a huge dramatic effect. Imagine...

61
00:04:29,143 --> 00:04:32,031
"We were together last night."

62
00:04:32,031 --> 00:04:36,071
"Not because she's my girlfriend,
but because she's my cook."

63
00:04:36,071 --> 00:04:37,616
Isn't that boring?

64
00:04:37,616 --> 00:04:38,943
Well, yes,

65
00:04:38,943 --> 00:04:42,490
and if you say she's a cook,
you have a lot of explaining to do.

66
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:45,309
Like... "why is she a cook?"

67
00:04:45,309 --> 00:04:47,859
"Does she cook well?"

68
00:04:47,859 --> 00:04:51,330
"She's still young.
Is she a cooking master boy?"

69
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:53,599
"Is she an anime character?"

70
00:04:53,599 --> 00:04:54,733
Right?

71
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:57,236
At least, if you say she's my girlfriend,

72
00:04:57,236 --> 00:04:59,137
they will easily get it.

73
00:05:04,810 --> 00:05:10,082
Oh Lord, do rich people think this way?

74
00:05:10,082 --> 00:05:12,583
They have defective minds.

75
00:05:16,722 --> 00:05:18,023
And you, Nero, first thing tomorrow,

76
00:05:18,023 --> 00:05:19,997
you'll take back everything you said.

77
00:05:19,997 --> 00:05:22,194
Explain to them
that I am not your girlfriend.

78
00:05:22,194 --> 00:05:24,162
I am your cook. I'm the cook of the Ferells.

79
00:05:24,162 --> 00:05:25,664
No.

80
00:05:25,664 --> 00:05:27,299
What do you mean "no"?

81
00:05:27,299 --> 00:05:29,668
He can't do that, Florence.

82
00:05:29,668 --> 00:05:34,306
If he does, he will lose his reputation.

83
00:05:34,306 --> 00:05:37,255
Then, he shouldn't have done that.

84
00:05:38,145 --> 00:05:41,680
They all lied just to ruin you.

85
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:43,282
And so?

86
00:05:43,282 --> 00:05:45,083
We will lie too?

87
00:05:45,083 --> 00:05:46,918
We will not tell the truth?

88
00:05:46,918 --> 00:05:50,522
We will level with them
because they don't play fair?

89
00:05:50,522 --> 00:05:53,163
It's more radical to be...

90
00:05:57,062 --> 00:05:58,734
honest.

91
00:05:59,695 --> 00:06:04,404
Okay, I'll be honest with you.

92
00:06:04,404 --> 00:06:09,574
I won't follow what you want,
and you'll follow me.

93
00:06:09,574 --> 00:06:14,177
From now on, act like my girlfriend.

94
00:06:16,782 --> 00:06:19,660
And why would I do that?

95
00:06:20,886 --> 00:06:23,755
You owe me three favors.

96
00:06:23,755 --> 00:06:27,225
Three chances
that you will follow whatever I like.

97
00:06:27,225 --> 00:06:32,264
No questions asked... no nothing.

98
00:06:32,264 --> 00:06:38,430
So, three minus one, two more favors to go.

99
00:06:53,358 --> 00:06:55,051
Come on, Florence,

100
00:06:55,051 --> 00:06:58,290
being Nero's girlfriend
isn't the worst thing in the world.

101
00:06:58,290 --> 00:07:00,258
There are far more worse things
in this world.

102
00:07:00,258 --> 00:07:04,456
There's a war in Europe, global warming,
and income inequality.

103
00:07:04,456 --> 00:07:07,332
Not to mention the rise of populism.

104
00:07:07,332 --> 00:07:10,569
Manchester United, LA Lakers.

105
00:07:10,569 --> 00:07:11,903
Exactly!

106
00:07:11,903 --> 00:07:13,839
Will you stop bothering me?

107
00:07:13,839 --> 00:07:16,742
But still, you have no choice.

108
00:07:16,742 --> 00:07:18,577
Can I use one of your favors, Nero?

109
00:07:18,577 --> 00:07:21,517
I'll just ask Florence
to do one of my assignments.

110
00:07:24,416 --> 00:07:26,685
You know, as long as you ask properly,

111
00:07:26,685 --> 00:07:30,222
I will help you with your assignment.

112
00:07:30,222 --> 00:07:33,592
Wow, Bro, if she'll do your assignment,

113
00:07:33,592 --> 00:07:36,151
then you'll end up owing her.

114
00:07:36,151 --> 00:07:37,822
Of course.

115
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:47,739
Guys!

116
00:07:47,739 --> 00:07:49,508
Something is happening.

117
00:07:49,508 --> 00:07:52,241
It's better if you come back.

118
00:07:53,311 --> 00:07:56,314
- Let's go.
- Okay, go.

119
00:08:02,454 --> 00:08:04,488
Hello, hello.

120
00:08:06,024 --> 00:08:08,526
Everyone, please settle down.

121
00:08:18,537 --> 00:08:22,207
It has come to my attention that someone here

122
00:08:22,207 --> 00:08:25,577
has photoshopped an image of another student

123
00:08:25,577 --> 00:08:31,883
to spread malicious rumors
about another student.

124
00:08:31,883 --> 00:08:36,154
If you read your student handbook,

125
00:08:36,154 --> 00:08:38,824
which I'm sure you all did,

126
00:08:38,824 --> 00:08:44,816
this is a clear violation of Chapter 7,
Section 3, and subsection C

127
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:50,434
that governs student conduct
here in our school.

128
00:08:50,434 --> 00:08:58,643
We do not spread disinformation
to ruin our fellow Gyronellan.

129
00:08:58,643 --> 00:09:01,213
No, no, no!

130
00:09:01,213 --> 00:09:03,547
A big no!

131
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:13,625
So, in light of recent events,

132
00:09:13,625 --> 00:09:19,364
we now declare Florence as the representative
of the Com Arts department.

133
00:09:19,364 --> 00:09:21,432
Yes!

134
00:09:53,574 --> 00:09:57,769
Thank you. Florence, care to join us?

135
00:09:57,769 --> 00:10:02,173
No thanks, Grandfather Garp.
I'll eat with Ma'am Serafica.

136
00:10:04,037 --> 00:10:06,918
Is it true that
you're the student representative of Com Arts?

137
00:10:06,919 --> 00:10:09,014
Yes.

138
00:10:09,014 --> 00:10:10,282
Are you happy?

139
00:10:10,282 --> 00:10:12,751
Yes, I am so happy.

140
00:10:12,751 --> 00:10:15,988
Are you happy that you're Nero's girlfriend?

141
00:10:21,718 --> 00:10:25,430
I know everything. They told me about it.

142
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:28,633
Your day was eventful.

143
00:10:28,633 --> 00:10:34,104
That's why you should teach them not to lie.

144
00:10:34,104 --> 00:10:35,639
Oh, you're right. Alright.

145
00:10:35,639 --> 00:10:37,307
It's true, we shouldn't tell a lie.

146
00:10:37,307 --> 00:10:40,377
But you know, Florence, sometimes in life,

147
00:10:40,377 --> 00:10:46,416
we have to compromise and improvise.

148
00:10:46,416 --> 00:10:50,087
And you, Nero,
what you did is very admirable.

149
00:10:50,087 --> 00:10:51,952
It's not the lying,

150
00:10:51,952 --> 00:10:55,342
but it's your instinct to save Florence
from someone

151
00:10:55,342 --> 00:10:57,879
who is destroying her character.

152
00:10:58,962 --> 00:11:01,899
Florence here is family. She's one of us.

153
00:11:01,899 --> 00:11:05,569
And it's our instinct to protect our own.

154
00:11:05,569 --> 00:11:09,618
She's family and we always protect our own.

155
00:11:14,611 --> 00:11:16,547
Hello, Mother. Hello, Father.

156
00:11:16,547 --> 00:11:19,316
Everything is okay here.

157
00:11:19,316 --> 00:11:23,186
<i>We're happy because
you're adapting to your university.</i>

158
00:11:23,186 --> 00:11:24,655
It's a celebration!

159
00:11:24,655 --> 00:11:25,789
A jubilation!

160
00:11:25,789 --> 00:11:29,226
Congratulations, my child. Congra...
Wait, what did she win?

161
00:11:29,226 --> 00:11:30,627
She's the head of her course.

162
00:11:30,627 --> 00:11:31,828
Wow. You're now the head...

163
00:11:31,828 --> 00:11:34,431
Congratulations on being
the head of your course.

164
00:11:34,431 --> 00:11:36,099
What's her course?

165
00:11:36,099 --> 00:11:37,935
It's Communication Arts.
You're something else.

166
00:11:37,935 --> 00:11:41,104
Are you the father of our daughter?

167
00:11:41,842 --> 00:11:47,703
Hey, Florence, you might become too busy
and forget about us.

168
00:11:47,703 --> 00:11:51,214
Is that possible when you're my family?

169
00:11:51,214 --> 00:11:54,887
Why, Florence, do you now
want a different family?

170
00:11:54,887 --> 00:11:57,090
Are you transferring to a different family?

171
00:11:57,090 --> 00:11:58,991
Mother is something else.

172
00:11:58,991 --> 00:12:00,293
Of course not.

173
00:12:00,293 --> 00:12:01,761
I'm just thinking,

174
00:12:01,761 --> 00:12:06,199
I can't handle it if you're far from me,
and the challenges in the school,

175
00:12:06,199 --> 00:12:08,909
if it weren't for the Ferells.

176
00:12:08,909 --> 00:12:13,139
It's difficult to believe,
but as time goes by,

177
00:12:13,139 --> 00:12:17,237
we're becoming a family too.

178
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:19,112
That's life, Florence.

179
00:12:19,112 --> 00:12:20,747
As the world goes bigger,

180
00:12:20,747 --> 00:12:24,817
more people will become part of our lives.

181
00:12:24,817 --> 00:12:29,648
I am confident that there'll be more people
you can see as your family

182
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:33,025
because you have a good heart.

183
00:12:33,025 --> 00:12:38,631
And they are slowly seeing
the goodness in you.

184
00:12:38,631 --> 00:12:42,468
Florence,
since you're part of the Ferell family,

185
00:12:42,468 --> 00:12:45,772
I hope they'll bequeath to you
even a bonsai plant.

186
00:12:45,772 --> 00:12:47,706
- You're really a fool!
- Why?

187
00:12:47,706 --> 00:12:49,509
I don't know about your father.

188
00:12:49,509 --> 00:12:51,400
Father is something else.

189
00:12:55,467 --> 00:12:56,985
Nero.

190
00:12:58,818 --> 00:13:00,610
What do you need?

191
00:13:02,235 --> 00:13:04,590
Don't hurt her.

192
00:13:04,590 --> 00:13:06,659
She's a good person.

193
00:13:06,659 --> 00:13:09,095
Don't hurt her.

194
00:13:09,095 --> 00:13:12,465
Why would I hurt Florence?

195
00:13:12,465 --> 00:13:15,902
I know why you did that earlier.

196
00:13:15,902 --> 00:13:18,891
You're trying to use Florence
to hurt Antonia.

197
00:13:19,839 --> 00:13:21,333
I supported you

198
00:13:21,334 --> 00:13:24,777
because you tried to protect Florence
from Camille.

199
00:13:24,777 --> 00:13:28,271
But I hope you don't use her
to get the girl you really want.

200
00:13:30,951 --> 00:13:35,013
First chance you get, you better cut it off.

201
00:13:35,013 --> 00:13:37,490
Stop pretending that she's your girlfriend,

202
00:13:37,490 --> 00:13:39,645
before someone gets hurt.

203
00:14:00,557 --> 00:14:02,812
Your hair smells good.

204
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:11,090
You've been thinking a lot of nonsense,

205
00:14:11,090 --> 00:14:14,018
that's why you're dreaming such things.

206
00:14:19,764 --> 00:14:23,268
What's this? A dream within a dream?

207
00:14:23,268 --> 00:14:25,670
Wake up, Florence. Wake up.

208
00:14:25,670 --> 00:14:27,797
- Wake up!
- Florence.

209
00:14:27,797 --> 00:14:29,307
What are you doing?

210
00:14:29,307 --> 00:14:32,076
Why are you hurting yourself?

211
00:14:32,076 --> 00:14:33,511
You're not true.

212
00:14:33,511 --> 00:14:35,780
I won't be intimate with you.

213
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:37,816
Because I'm a good, good, girl
in a good, good, world.

214
00:14:37,816 --> 00:14:40,785
And it's not a good, good thing
if you kiss me.

215
00:14:40,785 --> 00:14:44,355
Florence, I'm just waking you up.

216
00:14:44,355 --> 00:14:46,491
I've been knocking on your door.

217
00:14:46,491 --> 00:14:48,521
It seems you overslept.

218
00:15:07,779 --> 00:15:10,048
You're real! I'll just follow you.

219
00:15:10,048 --> 00:15:11,826
I'll just follow.

220
00:15:13,218 --> 00:15:14,652
I'll just follow!

221
00:15:14,652 --> 00:15:16,912
- I'll just follow!
- Hurry up!

222
00:15:21,392 --> 00:15:23,568
I slapped Nero.

223
00:15:25,141 --> 00:15:26,740
Let's go?

224
00:15:30,001 --> 00:15:33,905
<i>Wait, I dreamt about this.</i>

225
00:15:33,905 --> 00:15:35,473
<i>Is this still a dream?</i>

226
00:15:35,473 --> 00:15:36,941
Florence, we're late already.

227
00:15:36,941 --> 00:15:38,543
Let's go.

228
00:15:38,543 --> 00:15:41,302
- You go ahead.
- Florence, wait.

229
00:15:44,021 --> 00:15:46,551
The reason why I waited for you
is so you won't be late.

230
00:15:46,551 --> 00:15:48,115
So, let's go.

231
00:16:21,920 --> 00:16:23,746
Do you want to play some music?

232
00:16:26,224 --> 00:16:27,660
Go ahead.

233
00:16:29,127 --> 00:16:33,598
I thought you don't want others
to touch your car?

234
00:16:33,598 --> 00:16:37,996
That's okay, let's play some music.

235
00:16:53,918 --> 00:16:55,829
Look, Florence.

236
00:16:55,829 --> 00:16:59,170
The reason why I wanted to give you a ride,
is that I want to talk to you.

237
00:17:04,374 --> 00:17:06,233
Owen is right.

238
00:17:07,098 --> 00:17:09,335
I'm being unfair to you.

239
00:17:11,084 --> 00:17:12,780
Owen?

240
00:17:16,874 --> 00:17:21,577
He talked to me last night,
and warned me about you.

241
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,140
What for?

242
00:17:29,288 --> 00:17:33,569
He saw my real intention,
and why I declared you to be my girlfriend.

243
00:17:34,425 --> 00:17:38,561
Isn't it to debunk Camille's lies?

244
00:17:42,567 --> 00:17:44,296
Well...

245
00:17:45,236 --> 00:17:47,993
Are you telling me

246
00:17:47,993 --> 00:17:51,209
that you have a different reason
why you became a knight in shining armor

247
00:17:51,209 --> 00:17:53,313
during Agora day?

248
00:17:55,179 --> 00:17:57,280
Yes.

249
00:17:57,280 --> 00:17:59,548
It's a selfish reason.

250
00:18:00,752 --> 00:18:02,826
What's the reason?

251
00:18:05,590 --> 00:18:08,304
I want to get Antonia jealous.

252
00:18:12,942 --> 00:18:14,286
Oh.

253
00:18:16,349 --> 00:18:18,029
I see.

254
00:18:21,839 --> 00:18:25,710
You can get mad, you can slap me, punch me,

255
00:18:25,710 --> 00:18:28,945
or I'll get some of my things
and you can burn them again.

256
00:18:32,216 --> 00:18:33,711
Nero...

257
00:18:35,186 --> 00:18:37,488
thank you for your honesty.

258
00:18:37,488 --> 00:18:41,626
And like what Grandfather Garp said,
we're like family.

259
00:18:41,626 --> 00:18:46,197
So, if I can help you
achieve what your heart wants,

260
00:18:46,197 --> 00:18:50,835
and that is,
for Antonia to realize how amazing you are

261
00:18:50,835 --> 00:18:54,915
so she'll come back to you,

262
00:18:54,915 --> 00:18:59,674
then I'm more than willing to help you.

263
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:03,448
Thank you, Florence.

264
00:19:03,448 --> 00:19:04,982
Owen is right.

265
00:19:04,982 --> 00:19:06,885
You're a good person.

266
00:19:11,055 --> 00:19:12,619
Let's go?

267
00:20:14,785 --> 00:20:19,068
Shall we, my Chummy Pie?

268
00:20:27,798 --> 00:20:30,738
Florence, hi.

269
00:20:30,738 --> 00:20:32,470
Hi, Antonia.

270
00:20:32,470 --> 00:20:35,535
Nero, congratulations to you both.

271
00:20:35,535 --> 00:20:38,121
You guys make such a cute couple.

272
00:20:40,348 --> 00:20:41,646
Thank you.

273
00:20:41,646 --> 00:20:45,583
The first time I met you,
I knew you were a good person.

274
00:20:45,583 --> 00:20:46,653
To be honest,

275
00:20:46,653 --> 00:20:50,433
I'm supporting you ever since
you stood up to Aira and Camille.

276
00:20:50,433 --> 00:20:52,290
I've been hearing a lot of bad things
about them

277
00:20:52,290 --> 00:20:57,160
and it took somebody like you
to reveal their true colors.

278
00:20:57,160 --> 00:20:59,316
You're really lucky to have her, Nero.

279
00:20:59,316 --> 00:21:01,894
So, you better take good care of her.

280
00:21:04,345 --> 00:21:07,605
Anyway, I'll see you guys around.

281
00:21:11,274 --> 00:21:13,152
Let's go.

282
00:21:26,492 --> 00:21:27,992
<i>It looks effective.</i>

283
00:21:27,992 --> 00:21:31,498
<i>I saw a slight jealous moment
on Antonia's face.</i>

284
00:21:31,498 --> 00:21:32,523
<i>That's good.</i>

285
00:21:32,523 --> 00:21:35,169
<i>I hope she'll get jealous right away
and reconciles with Nero,</i>

286
00:21:35,169 --> 00:21:37,535
<i>so we can end this fool's first favor.</i>

287
00:21:37,535 --> 00:21:40,004
<i>And thank you, we'll go to the next favor.</i>

288
00:21:40,004 --> 00:21:41,106
<i>But wait,</i>

289
00:21:41,106 --> 00:21:43,407
<i>what if Antonia ignores the situation,</i>

290
00:21:43,407 --> 00:21:46,210
<i>and Nero will use his other favors?</i>

291
00:21:46,210 --> 00:21:47,878
<i>He'll kiss me in front of Antonia?</i>

292
00:21:47,878 --> 00:21:50,848
<i>Oh no, not my virgin lips, please.</i>

293
00:21:50,848 --> 00:21:52,750
<i>This is reserved for my future boyfriend.</i>

294
00:21:52,750 --> 00:21:56,587
<i>My future real boyfriend
who will really love me.</i>

295
00:21:56,587 --> 00:21:59,990
<i>But if this fool will court me...</i>

296
00:22:02,627 --> 00:22:03,803
<i>Why not?</i>

297
00:22:03,803 --> 00:22:05,850
<i>Should I be choosy?</i>

298
00:22:10,034 --> 00:22:12,436
Do you want to make it real
that we're in a relationship?

299
00:22:12,436 --> 00:22:13,912
<i>Oh my...</i>

300
00:22:13,912 --> 00:22:17,688
<i>Does Nero have telepathic skills
that he can read my mind?</i>

301
00:22:19,310 --> 00:22:21,410
<i>Does he want to kiss me?</i>

302
00:22:22,280 --> 00:22:25,283
You're holding my hand so tightly.

303
00:22:25,283 --> 00:22:27,318
You can let go now.

304
00:22:27,318 --> 00:22:31,902
No one... is looking.

305
00:22:34,692 --> 00:22:36,060
How should I know?

306
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:39,930
Of course, I'm already immersed
in the role of your fake girlfriend.

307
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:41,388
Okay.

308
00:22:47,104 --> 00:22:49,540
Is this the feeling of being used?

309
00:22:49,540 --> 00:22:53,269
If I don't owe you any favor,
you're nothing to me.

310
00:23:02,316 --> 00:23:03,888
Antonia.

311
00:23:05,389 --> 00:23:09,076
What? You'll just let them be?

312
00:23:11,084 --> 00:23:12,834
What do you mean?

313
00:23:14,732 --> 00:23:17,098
I'm sure you're not stupid.

314
00:23:17,098 --> 00:23:18,299
Do you really think

315
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:20,848
that Nero will just have
a new girlfriend overnight?

316
00:23:20,848 --> 00:23:25,402
I'm not one to make silly assumptions
when it comes to other people.

317
00:23:25,402 --> 00:23:28,590
The fact is, Nero and I are over.

318
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:31,574
So, he can do whatever he wants.

319
00:23:31,574 --> 00:23:35,541
If there's something that bothers me,
that's you.

320
00:23:41,691 --> 00:23:43,026
Me?

321
00:23:43,026 --> 00:23:44,827
Why are you telling me this?

322
00:23:44,827 --> 00:23:45,734
I thought you'd be interested

323
00:23:45,734 --> 00:23:48,935
to know the real score
between Nero and Florence.

324
00:23:48,935 --> 00:23:54,102
And I thought you're interested to know

325
00:23:54,102 --> 00:23:57,010
that all of this is just an act.

326
00:23:57,010 --> 00:23:59,876
Well, thank you for the information, Owen,

327
00:23:59,876 --> 00:24:03,613
but it doesn't take a genius
to realize what Nero is doing.

328
00:24:03,613 --> 00:24:06,159
He's simply protecting Florence

329
00:24:06,159 --> 00:24:10,086
when Aira and Camille
were destroying her reputation.

330
00:24:10,086 --> 00:24:12,541
But what I don't understand is...

331
00:24:12,541 --> 00:24:15,207
why are you guys protecting her?

332
00:24:15,207 --> 00:24:17,784
Who is she in your lives?

333
00:24:18,828 --> 00:24:20,721
She's our cook.

334
00:24:22,049 --> 00:24:24,266
Cook?

335
00:24:24,266 --> 00:24:25,734
Yes.

336
00:24:25,734 --> 00:24:28,169
Not any ordinary cook.

337
00:24:28,169 --> 00:24:31,022
She's the cook
who changed everything in the mansion.

338
00:24:32,641 --> 00:24:35,277
What do you mean?

339
00:24:35,277 --> 00:24:38,980
Well, ordinarily,
no one stays long in the mansion

340
00:24:38,980 --> 00:24:41,116
no matter how good they are.

341
00:24:41,116 --> 00:24:43,853
You know us Ferells.

342
00:24:44,953 --> 00:24:49,580
But when she came, she changed everything.

343
00:24:51,226 --> 00:24:53,627
He still can't get it.

344
00:24:59,067 --> 00:25:01,636
What do you call a group of dogs?

345
00:25:01,636 --> 00:25:04,354
- What?
- Aso-ciation.

346
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:07,609
- That's possible.
- Nice. Nice.

347
00:25:07,609 --> 00:25:09,778
Tough crowd. Tough crowd.

348
00:25:09,778 --> 00:25:11,346
One more. Knock-knock.

349
00:25:11,346 --> 00:25:12,514
Who's there?

350
00:25:12,514 --> 00:25:14,299
A lot of men.

351
00:25:20,822 --> 00:25:22,724
<i>She's special.</i>

352
00:25:22,724 --> 00:25:25,460
<i>She makes you see things differently.</i>

353
00:25:25,460 --> 00:25:28,696
<i>She can show that the world is colorful.</i>

354
00:25:28,696 --> 00:25:31,015
<i>She's not afraid to show her heart.</i>

355
00:25:35,804 --> 00:25:38,006
She makes you hopeful.

356
00:25:38,006 --> 00:25:40,375
She makes you brave.

357
00:25:40,375 --> 00:25:44,913
Brave enough that you can be happy.

358
00:25:44,913 --> 00:25:47,600
And she makes you understand
that to be happy...

359
00:25:47,601 --> 00:25:52,987
you have
to embrace it, grab it, and choose it.

360
00:25:52,987 --> 00:25:57,048
And when the opportunity comes,
you shouldn't be scared.

361
00:25:58,026 --> 00:26:01,529
Are you telling me all this...

362
00:26:01,529 --> 00:26:03,954
because you want me to break them apart?

363
00:26:04,824 --> 00:26:11,272
You want me to go back to Nero
so they can stop pretending.

364
00:26:11,272 --> 00:26:14,042
Because you're the one who likes Florence.

365
00:26:14,042 --> 00:26:17,212
You're the one who really likes her.

366
00:26:17,212 --> 00:26:21,459
And you're jealous because
Nero is playing the role of the boyfriend,

367
00:26:21,459 --> 00:26:24,619
the role that you wish
you could be playing instead.

368
00:26:24,619 --> 00:26:27,489
I thought you don't like making assumptions
about other people.

369
00:26:27,489 --> 00:26:28,957
You're right.

370
00:26:28,957 --> 00:26:31,493
I'm not one to make assumptions,

371
00:26:31,493 --> 00:26:36,367
but what I can only say to you
is be careful, Owen.

372
00:26:38,466 --> 00:26:41,102
This is a dangerous playground
that you're in.

373
00:26:41,102 --> 00:26:43,838
And it looks like you and Nero
are about to be involved

374
00:26:43,838 --> 00:26:46,914
in a seriously complicated situation.

375
00:27:14,669 --> 00:27:17,338
Florence, hi.

376
00:27:17,338 --> 00:27:18,873
Hello.

377
00:27:18,873 --> 00:27:21,709
Hello to our Com Arts representative,

378
00:27:21,709 --> 00:27:23,411
by the way, they are the representatives

379
00:27:23,411 --> 00:27:25,647
of the different sections of Com Arts.

380
00:27:25,647 --> 00:27:31,719
And we are all here today
for our first departmental consultation.

381
00:27:33,121 --> 00:27:34,609
I thought no one will come

382
00:27:34,609 --> 00:27:36,958
but it's a good thing
that we're all here right now.

383
00:27:36,958 --> 00:27:38,626
Of course, Ms. Florence.

384
00:27:38,626 --> 00:27:41,586
Oh, don't call me Miss.
Let's not be too formal.

385
00:27:41,586 --> 00:27:47,335
We're all students here, and we all fart.

386
00:27:47,335 --> 00:27:49,776
There you go. Of course, speaking of plans...

387
00:27:49,776 --> 00:27:53,617
Yes, I have plans.
Actually, I have a lot of plans.

388
00:27:53,617 --> 00:27:57,309
Because based on my observation
in this university these past few days,

389
00:27:57,309 --> 00:27:59,926
I have some ideas
that I want to share with you

390
00:27:59,926 --> 00:28:02,484
so that our student life can be improved.

391
00:28:02,484 --> 00:28:05,019
First, I saw the hangout area
of GU Com Arts Club

392
00:28:05,019 --> 00:28:07,185
and it needs a lot of improvement.

393
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:09,557
That's why I will ask for a budget
from the student council

394
00:28:09,557 --> 00:28:10,692
so we renovate it.

395
00:28:10,692 --> 00:28:12,104
And I also want to apply

396
00:28:12,104 --> 00:28:14,963
Google's work-life balance environment
to the department.

397
00:28:14,963 --> 00:28:17,499
In our case, school-life balance.

398
00:28:17,499 --> 00:28:20,607
I also thought of an anti-bullying platform

399
00:28:20,607 --> 00:28:23,876
because it's a rampant problem in GU.

400
00:28:23,876 --> 00:28:28,421
So I'll ask IT College to create
a direct messaging app

401
00:28:28,421 --> 00:28:34,200
so that the anonymous students
can file reports and harassment

402
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:36,951
so we can investigate it.

403
00:28:36,951 --> 00:28:40,860
And I also have plans to revive our Book Club

404
00:28:40,860 --> 00:28:45,064
so we, the students,
can have personal interaction

405
00:28:45,064 --> 00:28:51,408
and rediscover the jewel of GU
which is our library.

406
00:28:54,736 --> 00:28:58,344
Are there any problems with my ideas?

407
00:28:58,344 --> 00:29:01,517
Are there things you don't like,
or do you want to add something?

408
00:29:01,517 --> 00:29:03,711
It's okay, Florence.

409
00:29:03,711 --> 00:29:09,334
Your ideas are good,
but it seems that's not what we're expecting

410
00:29:09,334 --> 00:29:12,992
to talk about in this meeting.

411
00:29:12,992 --> 00:29:15,803
Why? What should we talk about?

412
00:29:15,803 --> 00:29:18,293
- About the Grand GU Ball.
- Yes.

413
00:29:18,293 --> 00:29:20,261
Grand GU Ball?

414
00:29:20,261 --> 00:29:22,363
Weren't you informed, Florence?

415
00:29:22,363 --> 00:29:26,303
It's the most important event
here in GU, right?

416
00:29:27,702 --> 00:29:29,764
And it's coming up already.

417
00:29:29,764 --> 00:29:32,206
So as our student representative,

418
00:29:32,206 --> 00:29:35,209
I think it's a good idea
that we should all brainstorm

419
00:29:35,209 --> 00:29:36,846
for this upcoming event.

420
00:29:36,846 --> 00:29:41,651
I'm sorry, Florence,
but the Grand GU Ball is not just a party.

421
00:29:41,651 --> 00:29:44,320
Yes, and this year is very important.

422
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:48,909
That's because the Com Arts are
the designated host of this grand event.

423
00:29:51,268 --> 00:29:55,532
Well... If that's how important it is,

424
00:29:55,532 --> 00:29:57,600
the floor is now open for suggestions.

425
00:29:57,600 --> 00:29:59,981
Do you have ideas?

426
00:29:59,981 --> 00:30:03,640
Why don't we make a localized version
of Coachella?

427
00:30:03,640 --> 00:30:05,809
Let's call it a music festival

428
00:30:05,809 --> 00:30:10,647
so it wouldn't be too boring ball
and not always formal.

429
00:30:10,647 --> 00:30:14,651
Bad idea. I mean, it's so hot in our country.

430
00:30:14,651 --> 00:30:16,720
We'll smell like onions.

431
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:20,623
Besides, after Astroworld,
I don't think it's a good idea.

432
00:30:20,623 --> 00:30:22,448
Let's go for something vintage.

433
00:30:22,448 --> 00:30:23,993
A Retro Ball.

434
00:30:23,993 --> 00:30:26,863
No way. It smells like the nostalgia
of grandmother and grandfather.

435
00:30:26,863 --> 00:30:30,166
As for me, I suggest
that we go for "classic eleganza",

436
00:30:30,166 --> 00:30:32,702
like the 1800s Victorian Party.

437
00:30:32,702 --> 00:30:36,473
It's so hard to dance
with a full skirt and petticoat.

438
00:30:36,473 --> 00:30:37,874
I have a better one.

439
00:30:37,874 --> 00:30:41,010
Why not let's just make a Filipino version
of "Le Bal"?

440
00:30:41,010 --> 00:30:42,545
That's going to be a show-off.

441
00:30:42,545 --> 00:30:43,880
Do you want to show off?

442
00:30:43,880 --> 00:30:48,017
How about our own version
of the famous Il Ballo del Doge?

443
00:30:48,017 --> 00:30:51,121
Yes, and let's have Pierre Gagnaire's
fusion cuisine.

444
00:30:51,121 --> 00:30:57,260
I love his foie gras soup with lentil gnocci
and balsamic onions.

445
00:30:57,260 --> 00:31:01,131
Or the dish inspired
by that Chinese French Artist.

446
00:31:01,131 --> 00:31:02,565
The Zao Wou Ki.

447
00:31:02,565 --> 00:31:03,883
- That's it.
- Yes.

448
00:31:03,883 --> 00:31:08,438
The beet and orange-infused daikon
with onion puree.

449
00:31:08,438 --> 00:31:11,741
That's okay,
as long as the wine is Romaneè-Conti.

450
00:31:11,741 --> 00:31:13,615
Perfecto.

451
00:31:23,920 --> 00:31:25,553
Let's go.

452
00:31:37,367 --> 00:31:39,002
All your suggestions are good.

453
00:31:39,002 --> 00:31:41,838
I'll think about it and study all of them.

454
00:31:41,838 --> 00:31:45,047
I'll make sure to integrate
all your suggestions.

455
00:31:49,012 --> 00:31:50,596
Let's go.

456
00:32:03,326 --> 00:32:05,195
Florence, wait, wait, wait.

457
00:32:05,195 --> 00:32:07,530
You left something.

458
00:32:07,530 --> 00:32:10,667
Your hair, it's so long.

459
00:32:10,667 --> 00:32:13,303
- Lina.
- It might get tangled.

460
00:32:13,303 --> 00:32:15,346
- Bye.
- Bye.

461
00:32:18,463 --> 00:32:22,283
So, how's your student consultation?

462
00:32:23,112 --> 00:32:24,385
What?

463
00:32:25,346 --> 00:32:30,486
Is this included in our pretend relationship?

464
00:32:30,486 --> 00:32:34,624
Pretend that you're concerned
with what happened with my day?

465
00:32:34,624 --> 00:32:36,525
You know, no need.

466
00:32:36,525 --> 00:32:39,995
I know you're not interested
in what's happening in my life.

467
00:32:39,995 --> 00:32:42,898
There's no difference if lightning strikes me

468
00:32:42,898 --> 00:32:44,866
or the crocodiles will eat me up.

469
00:32:44,866 --> 00:32:46,268
We're just pretending

470
00:32:46,268 --> 00:32:50,078
so we should mind our own business
and I know that.

471
00:33:00,824 --> 00:33:02,475
I'm sorry.

472
00:33:04,366 --> 00:33:07,383
You're asking nicely,

473
00:33:07,383 --> 00:33:09,991
and I answered you with those things.

474
00:33:10,892 --> 00:33:14,086
I don't know why I answered you that way.

475
00:33:14,086 --> 00:33:17,265
Maybe I'm just pressured
with being the student representative.

476
00:33:17,265 --> 00:33:22,637
Think about it,
I thought of a lot of ideas and projects

477
00:33:22,637 --> 00:33:25,540
to make our university better,

478
00:33:25,540 --> 00:33:29,144
but then all they want to talk about
is just one thing,

479
00:33:29,144 --> 00:33:31,947
the Grand GU Ball.

480
00:33:31,947 --> 00:33:33,535
What hurts the most,

481
00:33:33,535 --> 00:33:36,518
I don't understand anything
about what they're talking about.

482
00:33:36,518 --> 00:33:39,393
They're like aliens with alien tongues.

483
00:33:39,393 --> 00:33:45,909
What's that,
Coachella, Astroworld, Le Bal...

484
00:33:46,995 --> 00:33:50,762
Il Ballo del... Doge?

485
00:33:50,762 --> 00:33:51,863
That's it.

486
00:33:51,863 --> 00:33:53,768
And there's something more.

487
00:33:53,768 --> 00:33:57,937
They're talking about that Pierre Gagnaire
as if it's their neighbor

488
00:33:57,937 --> 00:34:00,988
when I don't even know who that is.
I don't have any idea.

489
00:34:00,988 --> 00:34:02,643
Who is that?

490
00:34:05,046 --> 00:34:07,344
Maybe this is my karma.

491
00:34:07,344 --> 00:34:09,507
I'm acting like a smart alec.

492
00:34:14,890 --> 00:34:17,559
Coachella is a popular music festival.

493
00:34:17,559 --> 00:34:21,469
Coachella Valley Music and Arts Festival
that is held in California.

494
00:34:21,469 --> 00:34:23,531
Maybe that's why they also said Astroworld,

495
00:34:23,531 --> 00:34:27,260
because that's a perfect example of
a music festival that didn't go well.

496
00:34:29,315 --> 00:34:30,656
A stampede can happen,

497
00:34:30,656 --> 00:34:33,808
or people can get hurt,
like what happened in Astroworld.

498
00:34:33,808 --> 00:34:36,229
Le Bal is short for Le Bal des Debutantse.

499
00:34:36,229 --> 00:34:37,879
That was formally known as Crillon Ball,

500
00:34:37,879 --> 00:34:39,729
which happens every year in France.

501
00:34:39,729 --> 00:34:41,750
It's like the Filipino debut party,

502
00:34:41,750 --> 00:34:45,654
and the children of famous
and well-known people are invited.

503
00:34:45,654 --> 00:34:47,993
The Il Ballo del Doge is a masquerade ball

504
00:34:47,993 --> 00:34:49,748
that is held in Venetian Palace

505
00:34:49,748 --> 00:34:54,329
that is called Palazzo Pisani Moretta
in the Grand Canal.

506
00:34:54,329 --> 00:35:01,626
So, I assume that's the grand canal
in Venice, Italy, right?

507
00:35:01,626 --> 00:35:03,371
Because with the tone of your voice,

508
00:35:03,371 --> 00:35:05,941
it's impossible that it's just the canals
around the area

509
00:35:05,941 --> 00:35:10,045
or Mall of Taguig or whatever city.

510
00:35:10,045 --> 00:35:11,446
Whatever they call the canal there.

511
00:35:11,446 --> 00:35:12,770
Exactly.

512
00:35:12,770 --> 00:35:15,350
And Pierre Gagnaire is a famous chef.

513
00:35:15,350 --> 00:35:18,653
But if you'll ask me, he is overrated.

514
00:35:18,653 --> 00:35:23,945
I think you're a better cook compared to him.

515
00:35:28,304 --> 00:35:33,048
Thank you for your vote of confidence.

516
00:35:33,048 --> 00:35:35,403
If there's something you don't understand
in this world,

517
00:35:35,403 --> 00:35:37,706
don't hesitate to ask me.

518
00:35:37,706 --> 00:35:39,562
That's the least I can do.

519
00:35:40,444 --> 00:35:42,163
Thank you.

520
00:35:48,929 --> 00:35:50,652
It's still early.

521
00:35:50,652 --> 00:35:52,554
Let's eat first.

522
00:35:52,554 --> 00:35:54,812
Huh? Where?

523
00:36:12,803 --> 00:36:14,241
Thank you.

524
00:36:15,744 --> 00:36:17,491
Here, Ma'am.

525
00:36:20,949 --> 00:36:22,749
Go ahead and order.

526
00:36:31,192 --> 00:36:32,961
Soup?

527
00:36:32,961 --> 00:36:35,766
450 pesos per bowl?

528
00:36:35,766 --> 00:36:38,931
What's that?
Do the ingredients have gold dust?

529
00:36:38,931 --> 00:36:40,726
Why is it so expensive?

530
00:36:42,170 --> 00:36:45,741
Just order, and I will pay for it.

531
00:36:46,841 --> 00:36:49,310
I can't help but look at the price.

532
00:36:49,310 --> 00:36:51,788
It makes me feel guilty to eat...

533
00:36:54,916 --> 00:37:02,048
Oh my... Pork adobo, 1,000 pesos per order?

534
00:37:02,048 --> 00:37:04,710
That's already good for 10 people.

535
00:37:08,363 --> 00:37:11,170
Florence, I'm hungry, okay?

536
00:37:11,170 --> 00:37:14,001
Stop overreacting. I'll pay for it.

537
00:37:14,001 --> 00:37:16,237
Overreacting, Nero? Me?

538
00:37:16,237 --> 00:37:17,439
They're overpriced.

539
00:37:17,439 --> 00:37:18,540
No!

540
00:37:18,540 --> 00:37:20,175
This is very wrong.

541
00:37:20,175 --> 00:37:22,944
Very, very, very, very, wrong.

542
00:37:22,944 --> 00:37:26,114
And besides, I'm not your real girlfriend

543
00:37:26,114 --> 00:37:28,349
for you to spend on me this much.

544
00:37:28,349 --> 00:37:31,119
You should spend it on your real girlfriend.

545
00:37:31,119 --> 00:37:33,945
You should invest in her, not me.

546
00:37:35,362 --> 00:37:40,640
Well, even if I become
your real girlfriend...

547
00:37:42,831 --> 00:37:45,033
I still can't eat in a place like this, Nero.

548
00:37:45,033 --> 00:37:46,634
This is a luxury, Nero.

549
00:37:46,634 --> 00:37:49,275
And besides, there are a lot of
cheap eateries in the area

550
00:37:49,275 --> 00:37:51,050
that are delicious.

551
00:37:51,050 --> 00:37:54,576
So, if you want to eat, go ahead.
I will not eat here.

552
00:37:54,576 --> 00:37:58,103
Whatever is left, I'll donate to charity.

553
00:38:06,921 --> 00:38:08,923
Okay fine,

554
00:38:08,923 --> 00:38:12,470
where is this place accepted
by your moral standards?

555
00:38:29,878 --> 00:38:31,146
That's it.

556
00:38:31,146 --> 00:38:33,781
That's the food that you can eat
without your conscience bothering you,

557
00:38:33,781 --> 00:38:35,617
unlike the place you brought me earlier.

558
00:38:35,617 --> 00:38:38,253
I think they're scammers.
They charge you so much.

559
00:38:38,253 --> 00:38:41,160
They're higher than our electricity bill.

560
00:38:43,925 --> 00:38:47,661
Hey, remember you asked me earlier
where I want to eat?

561
00:38:47,661 --> 00:38:49,397
Well, this is it.

562
00:38:49,397 --> 00:38:51,432
We're here.

563
00:38:51,432 --> 00:38:53,501
Promise, Nero, it's delicious.

564
00:38:53,501 --> 00:38:54,849
Just try it.

565
00:38:54,849 --> 00:38:58,640
First, Barbecue.

566
00:38:58,640 --> 00:39:00,975
It's delicious.
This is one of my favorites here.

567
00:39:00,975 --> 00:39:03,745
- Come on, try it.
- I don't eat that.

568
00:39:03,745 --> 00:39:05,013
You're such a killjoy.

569
00:39:05,013 --> 00:39:06,615
Nero, I know that you're a rich kid,

570
00:39:06,615 --> 00:39:09,150
but you should also try this kind of food.

571
00:39:09,150 --> 00:39:10,885
Come on.

572
00:39:10,885 --> 00:39:13,688
I told you I don't eat that.

573
00:39:13,688 --> 00:39:16,491
Well, you're nothing.

574
00:39:16,491 --> 00:39:20,762
I thought you eat food like this
since you grew up in a barrio.

575
00:39:20,762 --> 00:39:23,354
It turns out I'm wrong.

576
00:39:24,057 --> 00:39:29,526
Mister, give me one isaw,
betamax, and chicken ass.

577
00:39:34,108 --> 00:39:35,343
What happened?

578
00:39:35,343 --> 00:39:36,945
I thought you don't eat food like this?

579
00:39:36,945 --> 00:39:38,810
Did you get hungry?

580
00:39:39,614 --> 00:39:41,916
You were forced?

581
00:39:41,916 --> 00:39:43,918
I don't eat barbecue,

582
00:39:43,918 --> 00:39:46,154
but I eat isaw, betamax, and chicken ass.

583
00:39:46,154 --> 00:39:47,689
Those are my favorite.

584
00:39:47,689 --> 00:39:51,359
That's our usual food
on the medical mission with dad.

585
00:39:51,359 --> 00:39:55,396
Wow, in fairness,
you've memorized all the names.

586
00:39:55,396 --> 00:39:57,365
To be fair, I wasn't expecting that.

587
00:39:57,365 --> 00:40:00,612
You're an expert
when it comes to grilling food.

588
00:40:03,002 --> 00:40:05,070
Are you smiling?

589
00:40:06,774 --> 00:40:09,477
He's more cowboy than me.

590
00:40:09,477 --> 00:40:14,816
So, his favorite fruit is rambutan.

591
00:40:14,816 --> 00:40:21,107
And it looks like his favorite food
is grilled stuff in Hepa Lane.

592
00:40:22,021 --> 00:40:24,125
Good job, Florencia,

593
00:40:24,125 --> 00:40:28,863
you're slowly solving Nero's mysterious side.

594
00:40:28,863 --> 00:40:31,199
Come on, you can ride with me to school.

595
00:40:31,199 --> 00:40:32,900
Let's go, Florence.

596
00:40:32,900 --> 00:40:35,912
Bro, I will bring Florence to school.

597
00:40:35,912 --> 00:40:37,605
I will.

598
00:40:37,605 --> 00:40:39,340
I'm the boyfriend.

599
00:40:39,340 --> 00:40:41,216
Do you mean fake boyfriend?

600
00:40:41,216 --> 00:40:43,396
I understand you're trying
to protect Florence,

601
00:40:43,396 --> 00:40:45,333
but this is getting ridiculous.

602
00:40:45,333 --> 00:40:47,215
Florence and I have an agreement.

603
00:40:47,215 --> 00:40:50,155
She agreed to help me, so don't meddle.

604
00:40:50,155 --> 00:40:53,568
- Dad!
- Wait, you shouldn't hurt her.

605
00:40:53,568 --> 00:40:54,889
He's my father.

606
00:40:54,889 --> 00:40:56,228
Still, Camille,

607
00:40:56,228 --> 00:40:59,287
even if he's your father,
he doesn't have a right to hurt you that way.

608
00:40:59,287 --> 00:41:01,195
Hey you, don't meddle.

609
00:41:01,195 --> 00:41:03,100
This is a family matter.

610
00:41:05,400 --> 00:41:07,681
There's trouble in Camille's school.

611
00:41:07,681 --> 00:41:10,579
I had a confrontation
with the grandsons of Don Ferell.

612
00:41:10,579 --> 00:41:13,850
A Ferell woman started it.

613
00:41:13,850 --> 00:41:15,657
A Ferell woman?

614
00:41:15,657 --> 00:41:16,953
What's that?

615
00:41:16,953 --> 00:41:18,521
Do you want to find out?

616
00:41:18,521 --> 00:41:19,856
There are lights too.

617
00:41:19,856 --> 00:41:21,297
Why do you have a comforter?

618
00:41:21,297 --> 00:41:24,211
Well, just spread it out.

619
00:41:24,211 --> 00:41:26,096
Lie down. I said lie down.

620
00:41:26,096 --> 00:41:27,768
Are you ready?

621
00:41:27,768 --> 00:41:30,524
- What?
- Are you ready?

622
00:41:30,524 --> 00:41:32,357
I'll count to three...

623
00:41:32,357 --> 00:41:36,182
One, two, three..

624
00:41:36,182 --> 00:41:38,583
- You're rude!
- Hey, what's that?
